       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,000 mg/day of scheduled acetaminophen is a dose that can cause liver injury. I don't know of a clinical scenario that justifies it, and you haven't given a rationale. I'd rather not put it in the system where it could be given to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a maximum-dose regimen.** Options are 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day).\n- **Add multimodal analgesia.** If the goal is better pain control, I can enter an adjunct such as an NSAID, if appropriate for this patient, alongside acetaminophen at a safe dose.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you think a nonstandard dose is truly needed, a pharmacist or toxicology consult can review it and support a documented override.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
